From f4913706cc44dbca179062770bb8ebae0c4f5a53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:02:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(update-pause): announce a carried turn's pause;
 its continuation names the paused notification turn

Follow-up to PR #1870 review nits (review 5886094345, t_01a1d331f7c35630):

1. A synthesized turn that runs over a paused marker and is itself paused for the next window left its
   interrupted action only as transcript context: the continuation note named just the original paused
   request. The hook now stamps the marker `carried_turn_paused` when the pause it pays is a carried one
   (the same condition that already skipped counting it again), and the continuation appends
   CARRIED_TURN_NOTE telling the model a notification turn was paused too and its partial work is above.
   A turn's own fresh marker (record_turn_start) clears the flag.
2. The carried turn never called announce_pause: pause_stands was keyed on its empty marker key, so Desktop
   got a plain message.complete for a turn paused for the update. Publication now keys on
   update_pause.effective_pause_key (own marker key, else the carried paused key; replaces
   prompt_turn._carried_pause_key so the hook and the publication share one definition). The in-place
   watcher is still started there only for a turn's own marker; a carried turn's is re-armed exactly once by
   _rearm_carried_pause_watcher.
3. Test: a user Stop (real session.interrupt RPC) of a carried turn after its hook paid the pause:
   user_stop_wins returns False, the paused request survives as core_update_pause with its prompt, the
   watcher is re-armed and in_place_resume_action says resume.

Proof: tests/tui_gateway/test_update_pause_superseded.py, 4 new tests; the announce and the
carried_turn_paused/note tests fail before (announce_pause never called; no flag) and pass after, the Stop
test pins existing behaviour (18 passed). 129 test files referencing update_pause/turn_marker/prompt_turn/
session_auto_continue: 2536 passed, 2 failed in tests/gateway/test_kanban_restart_continuation.py, which
fail identically on the unchanged base (worker_account_boards refuses registration in the real worker
inventory on this worker node).
